---
// INC-261: captioned-image partial for case-study media (hero, problem visual,
// research artifacts, process grid, outcome visual) and home photography (hero
// portrait, about photo). This ticket ships the partial only — consumers integrate
// in later tickets, so no route renders it yet.
// a11y contract: `alt` is required and must describe the image — empty/decorative
// alt is out of contract (a decorative image doesn't belong in <figure>, which
// asserts content; use a plain <img alt=""> outside this partial). The optional
// caption supplements, never repeats, the alt. When both caption props are absent
// no <figcaption> is rendered. `captionLabel` is the bold lead line for two-part
// captions (e.g. "01 · Wireframe" over a description) — the process-grid shape.
// CONTRACT: plain <img> by design. astro:assets/<Image> is blocked on the sharp
// onlyBuiltDependencies follow-up (docs/follow-ups.md) and is its own
// separately-reviewed change; `src` is a URL string (public/ path).
// CONTRACT: `width`/`height` are intrinsic pixels, required so the browser
// reserves the aspect-ratio box before load (zero-JS CLS guard). `h-auto w-full`
// owns rendered size — sizing/layout belongs to the consumer's grid/flex cell;
// there is no size/variant/class API. Chrome is the single standardized
// rounded-2xl + 1px border-border, no shadow (the hi-fi's per-instance 16–24px
// radii are authoring artifacts, collapsed deliberately — stock scale per
// ADR-0004; shadows are reserved for cards and stat tiles).
// CONTRACT: `loading` defaults to lazy; above-fold consumers (case-study hero,
// home portrait) pass loading="eager".
// Figcaption classes are verbatim from prose.css `.prose figure > figcaption`
// (mt-3 text-caption text-muted-foreground) so Figure renders identically inside
// the case-study .prose scope and outside it (home); the in-prose duplicate
// application is same-value (utilities beat @layer components). The label's
// text-foreground/font-semibold sits on the default surface pair — no new
// contrast proof needed.
// Zero-hydration by contract (B4): no client:* directives, no <style>/<script>
// blocks. Byte-parity discipline: the template is a verbatim copy (text-node line
// structure matters under compressHTML) — commentary stays in frontmatter, never
// in the template.
interface Props {
	src: string;
	alt: string;
	width: number;
	height: number;
	captionLabel?: string;
	caption?: string;
	loading?: 'eager' | 'lazy';
}

const { src, alt, width, height, captionLabel, caption, loading = 'lazy' } = Astro.props;
---

<figure>
	<img src={src} alt={alt} width={width} height={height} loading={loading} class="h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-border" />
	{
		(captionLabel || caption) && (
			<figcaption class="mt-3 text-caption text-muted-foreground">
				{captionLabel && <span class="block font-semibold text-foreground">{captionLabel}</span>}
				{caption}
			</figcaption>
		)
	}
</figure>
